+# Errata of the frozen paper (draft 9)
+
+The paper is frozen after draft 9 and takes errata only (`docs/PRACTICES.md`, "The paper frozen after draft 9"; P-203):
+a mathematical error found by anyone gets a dated correction, and nothing else is written in. Its text and its PDF are
+not edited; each entry here is dated.
+
+## 2026-11-14 — two citations with later arcs, set out for main (register row P-319; the building session's card C20)
+
+The register's row P-319 names two arcs the paper cites that have successors. Each is set out below in the paper's words
+and the successor's; **no correction is entered**: whether either is an error of the paper is main's to decide, and an
+entry follows that decision.
+
+| the paper cites | the paper's words | the successor's words |
+|---|---|---|
+| B1479 (§ 2, `tex/sections/s02_grammar_seed.tex`) | "The place where a hand can be registered on a spin structure (B1479, B1481) is generated by the moves." | B1662's page: "**B1479:** \"not yet generated\" superseded; P1–P3 stand."; its verdict line: "Re-graded: B1482, B1479 (wording)" |
+| B1656 (§ 5, `tex/sections/s05_couplings.tex`) | "In the twisted frame of B1656, under equal framed data, one Higgs keeps the sectors' values of $t+1/t$ within a factor $4$, exactly" (the proposition "The twisted half bound; B1658") | B1658's page: "So \"one Higgs, under equal framed data, in B1656's frame\" is refuted — a scoreboard entry beside the SM seat's W88 and W90, not a closed door" |
+
+The paper already cites B1658 by name in the second row. The generator the row asks for is
+`scripts/checks/supersession_tier.py`: run with `--p9`, it lists every line of a later arc that names an arc the paper
+cites together with a word of supersession, 65 lines on 2026-11-14, these two pairs among them. Each is a line to read,
+not a finding.
